# [O-29] pcrec-bench 2026-09-16: three blocks, each carrying its own
# `provenance` sub-block as the LAST content of its block. Before the
# fix, `--list-source`'s `#section provenance` carried only the LAST
# block's record — the others vanished, exit 0, no diagnostic.
#
# The real mechanism (found by reading `src/parse/rxt_source.c`, not
# assumed from the bench's own hypothesis): it is NOT the arrival of the
# next `pattern`/`pattern-esc` opener that drops the record — that path
# runs the ordinary dedent-pop while loop, which calls `RXT_CLOSE_FRAME`
# (and therefore `close_section_frame`) correctly, exactly as it always
# has. It is a BLANK line or a COMMENT line closing the attachment
# first (S0's own rule — "a BLANK and a COMMENT each close every open
# attachment") that skipped the macro entirely, resetting `ndepth = 1`
# directly. Since two `pattern` blocks are ordinarily separated by a
# blank line (or, as here, sometimes a comment), the shape reproduces on
# essentially any real multi-block file that uses `provenance`.
#
# This fixture exercises all THREE closing sites in one file: block 1's
# provenance closes via a BLANK line, block 2's via a COMMENT line, block
# 3's via END OF FILE (the one site that was never broken — a fixed-point
# control proving the other two moved to match it, not the reverse).
# `tag t1` sits BEFORE block 1's `provenance`, per the bench's own
# observation that a `tag` line AFTER a block's provenance suppresses the
# drop (it triggers the correctly-working dedent-pop path); here it sits
# on the side that does NOT mask anything.
#
# Every block carries the full REQUIRED set for BLOCK-scope provenance
# (`source`, `retrieved`, `license`, `fidelity` — the PROVENANCE schema
# rows' own `required`/`required-if parent == block` constraints; without
# them the file would be REFUSED outright, which is a different failure
# mode from the silent drop this fixture is for).
pattern p1 a
tag t1
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license MIT
  fidelity verbatim

pattern p2 b
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license MIT
  fidelity adapted
  adaptation trimmed the trailing anchor for this corpus
# a comment, not a blank line, separates block 2 from block 3
pattern p3 c
provenance
  source authored
  retrieved 2026-09-16
  license MIT
  fidelity verbatim
